{"name":"Annular","hex":"#e17861","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"annular","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Pertaining to, or having the form of, a ring: in the shape of an annulus.","Banded or marked with circles."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/annular"}],"entries":[{"title":"Intervertebral disc","blocks":[{"text":"An intervertebral disc, also spelled intervertebral disk, lies between adjacent vertebrae in the vertebral column. Each disc forms a fibrocartilaginous joint, to allow slight movement of the vertebrae, to act as a ligament to hold the vertebrae together, and to function as a shock absorber for the spine."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/716_Intervertebral_Disk.svg/330px-716_Intervertebral_Disk.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Intervertebral_disc"},{"title":"Common tendinous ring","blocks":[{"text":"The common tendinous ring, also known as the annulus of Zinn or annular tendon, is a ring of fibrous tissue surrounding the optic nerve at its entrance at the apex of the orbit. It is the common origin of the four recti muscles of the group of extraocular muscles."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Eyemuscles.png/330px-Eyemuscles.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Common_tendinous_ring"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Cervical_vertebra_english.png/500px-Cervical_vertebra_english.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Cervical_vertebra_english.png/1280px-Cervical_vertebra_english.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Cervical_vertebra_